/* ==================================================================== *
 * keywordEngine.js — a dynamic, self-building keyword + entity engine
 * for county / local-government text.
 *
 * What makes it "smart" without calling out to a model:
 *   • One compiled regex per run, with NAMED GROUPS, so a single pass
 *     tells you WHICH department a hit belongs to (no N regexes, no
 *     N passes over the text).
 *   • Morphology tolerance   — closure / closures / closed / closing
 *   • Orthography tolerance  — right-of-way == right of way == rightofway
 *   • Case-sensitive acronym lane (ROW, TIF, ADA) so plain "row" is ignored
 *   • Fuzzy recovery         — bounded Levenshtein rescues "detor",
 *                              "culvirt", "resurfaceing"
 *   • Negation / hedging     — "no lane closure", "meeting cancelled"
 *                              flips a hit's polarity instead of counting it
 *   • Weighted scoring       — multi-word phrases and rare terms outrank
 *                              generic ones; confidence is normalized
 *                              across departments, with a margin check
 *   • Urgency + action signals, deadline awareness
 *   • Vocabulary discovery   — proposes unseen capitalized phrases as
 *                              candidate keywords (the "learning" loop)
 *   • Runtime learning       — matcher.learn(category, term) recompiles
 *
 * Zero dependencies. Pure functions. Safe to run on every keystroke.
 * ==================================================================== */

